 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Ya'qub and his eyes are never drawn; no plate in 84-85. Light for «عسى الله أن يأتيني بهم جميعا», geometric for «إنه هو العليم الحكيم». Cut: «صبرا جميلا» and passage echoes. STAGING v4: At Ya'qub's tents in the desert (12:100). Ya'qub is only a blue drop labelled Ya'qub; his sons are a plain group of three (3 figures = a group, not their number). c1 (83): Ya'qub answers them (83:1, 83:7), then they turn and leave (83:8), so that no three figures stand on stage while the gloss on his three sons is shown (83:9-14: the three he hopes for are Yusuf, Binyamin and the eldest, none of them here) and Ya'qub's drop stands alone; a light plate from 83:9 (may Allah bring them all back; it starts before the Name) and a geometric plate for the All-Knowing, the Wise (83:15). Nothing glows on Ya'qub. c2 (84): his grief is shown only through his drop: it turns away from them and moves aside (84:1-2, both tafsirs: he turned away from them) and dips once, softly (84:4, his sorrow); nothing is drawn for the eyes turning white (84:7-10) or for weeping, and there is no plate. c3 (85): his sons speak to him (85:1, 85:6, 85:9); no plate on their oath."
 },
